# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public-release hardening (added at final cleanup, before making the
# repository public). The patterns below are deliberately specific: this
# repository legitimately tracks aggregate-result .csv files, database
# schema .sql files, and small non-personal reference .xlsx workbooks, so
# no blanket *.csv / *.sql / *.xlsx ignore is used.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Secrets and credentials (none are currently tracked; these are preventive)
.env.*
!.env.example
*.env
.envrc
secrets.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
service_account*.json
client_secret*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.aws/
.netrc
cookies.txt
*.cookies

# Collection workbooks (personal data; none currently present, preventive guard)
05_Data_Collection/Collection_Workbooks/*.xlsx

# Database dumps and local databases
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.bak

# Any raw / unprocessed collection folder anywhere in the tree
**/01_Raw/
**/Raw_Data/
**/Raw_Exports/

# Thesis manuscript drafting workspace.
# 10_Thesis_Writing/ contains AI-assisted working drafts, chapter source maps,
# QA files and .docx manuscript drafts, all superseded by the submitted thesis.
# They are kept on disk for the author but excluded from the public repository
# so that no superseded draft can be mistaken for the final research record.
# The authoritative research record is the submitted thesis; the authoritative
# in-repo numbers are the outputs under 09_Statistical_Analysis/, 12_Figures/
# and 13_Tables/.
10_Thesis_Writing/

# OS / editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
*.swp
